<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Input Sequence Formation</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in Subsections <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 UATD ‣ 3 Dataset ‣ Universal Retrieval for Multimodal Trajectory Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Problem Definition ‣ 4 Framework ‣ Universal Retrieval for Multimodal Trajectory Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we represent a state <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> using a screenshot, and each action <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed as a JSON object with three keys: <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">operation</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">value</span>, and <span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">target</span>. A trajectory subsequence <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau_{i:j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i:j}</annotation></semantics></math> or a full trajectory <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math> (or simply <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>) is composed of state-action pairs. To standardize the representation across different environments, we prepend the action space definition to <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau_{i:j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i:j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{i:j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i:j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the target side of retrieval, <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math> can be either a single state <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or a trajectory sequence with action definitions, denoted as <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{i:j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i:j}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the query side <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we prepend the retrieval query <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, which includes a task-specific instruction and trajectory description to <math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{i:j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i:j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix A Input Sequence Formation ‣ Universal Retrieval for Multimodal Trajectory Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> displays concrete examples, where <span id="A1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[image]</span> denotes image tokens.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Examples of model input representations for a state (<math id="A1.T7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>), an action (<math id="A1.T7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>), a trajectory sequence or subsequence with action definitions (<math id="A1.T7.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{i:j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i:j}</annotation></semantics></math>), and an augmented retrieval query (<math id="A1.T7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math>). The retrieval key <math id="A1.T7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{k}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of <math id="A1.T7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math> combined with either <math id="A1.T7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.T7.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{i:j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i:j}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the retrieval value <math id="A1.T7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is composed of either <math id="A1.T7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.T7.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{i:j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i:j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
